    <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Parent Resource Guide</h1>
        <p>Everything families need to know about Cub Scout Pack 3963 — communication, meetings, uniforms, advancement, safety, and how to get involved.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>How Pack 3963 Communicates</h2>
        <p>We use a combination of email, Scoutbook, and our pack website to keep families informed. Major announcements are posted on the homepage banner and emailed to all registered parents.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Email — weekly updates and reminders</li>
            <li>Scoutbook — advancement tracking and den communication</li>
            <li>Website — event details, resources, and pack-wide updates</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Meeting Expectations</h2>
        <p>Pack meetings occur monthly and include awards, activities, and announcements. Den meetings occur 1–2 times per month depending on the den.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Arrive on time</li>
            <li>Wear the appropriate uniform</li>
            <li>Parents remain on-site for Lions and Tigers</li>
            <li>Respectful behavior is expected from all scouts</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Uniform Guide</h2>
        <p>Uniforms help build pride and belonging. Each rank has its own color and insignia.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Lion — T-shirt and optional cap</li>
            <li>Tiger — Blue uniform shirt, neckerchief, slide</li>
            <li>Wolf — Blue uniform shirt, neckerchief, slide</li>
            <li>Bear — Blue uniform shirt, neckerchief, slide</li>
            <li>Webelos — Tan uniform shirt, neckerchief</li>
            <li>Arrow of Light — Tan uniform shirt, neckerchief</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Full uniform details are available on our <a href="resources.html">Resources page</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Advancement Overview</h2>
        <p>Scouts earn adventure loops and pins throughout the year. Advancement is tracked in Scoutbook and recognized at pack meetings.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Adventure loops/pins</li>
            <li>Rank requirements</li>
            <li>Pack awards and recognition</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Parent Participation</h2>
        <p>Parents are essential to the success of our pack. Opportunities include volunteering at events, helping with den activities, and joining the pack committee.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Safety & Youth Protection</h2>
        <p>All leaders are trained in Youth Protection. Parents should follow drop-off/pick-up guidelines and ensure scouts are supervised appropriately.</p>
    </section>

